From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:28:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] est: a supply net is never pending for parasitics
 re-estimation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Removing or inserting a buffer connects or disconnects its power pins,
so the supply nets were queued in parasitics_invalid_ by every such
edit, and updateParasitics() then ran delaysInvalidFromFanin() on them:
a visit of every pin on VDD and VSS, that is every cell in the design.
rsz's fullyRebuffer updates parasitics once per driver, so a netlist
whose synthesis buffers were kept paid it once per driver.

On a 1.9 M instance hierarchical design (XiangShan's XSTile parent, in
bazel-orfs), timing-driven global placement's first re-weight ground
over 5 h in fullyRebuffer, 151,500 of 1,515,054 pins in 2 h; perf put
99.8 % in updateParasitics -> delaysInvalidFromFanin ->
visitConnectedPins, and the estimator's debug log named VDD and VSS,
invalidated 95 times each in 4 minutes while every signal net appeared
once.

A supply net carries no estimated parasitics, so parasiticsInvalid()
skips it. TestEstimateParasitics.SupplyNetIsNotInvalidated fails
without the change (VDD pending) and passes with it; est's 15 tests
pass.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/est/src/EstimateParasitics.cpp         |  4 ++-
 src/est/test/cpp/TestEstimateParasitics.cc | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/est/src/EstimateParasitics.cpp b/src/est/src/EstimateParasitics.cpp
index 7df36e8a75..ce5769078b 100644
--- a/src/est/src/EstimateParasitics.cpp
+++ b/src/est/src/EstimateParasitics.cpp
@@ -1547,7 +1547,9 @@ bool EstimateParasitics::isSkipNet(const sta::Net* net) const
 void EstimateParasitics::parasiticsInvalid(const sta::Net* net)
 {
   odb::dbNet* db_net = db_network_->findFlatDbNet(net);
-  if (haveEstimatedParasitics() && db_net) {
+  // A supply net carries no estimated parasitics, and every cell's power pin
+  // is on it: invalidating its delays from fanin visits them all.
+  if (haveEstimatedParasitics() && db_net && !db_net->getSigType().isSupply()) {
     debugPrint(logger_,
                EST,
                "estimate_parasitics",
diff --git a/src/est/test/cpp/TestEstimateParasitics.cc b/src/est/test/cpp/TestEstimateParasitics.cc
index 6c286415b5..b6d0f09307 100644
--- a/src/est/test/cpp/TestEstimateParasitics.cc
+++ b/src/est/test/cpp/TestEstimateParasitics.cc
@@ -308,6 +308,42 @@ TEST_F(TestEstimateParasitics, IdealClockNetSkipsStaInvalidation)
   ep_.setIncrementalParasiticsEnabled(false);
 }
 
+// A supply net is never pending: removing or inserting a buffer touches its
+// power pins, and updateParasitics() would then invalidate delays from the
+// fanin of every power pin in the design, once per edit.
+TEST_F(TestEstimateParasitics, SupplyNetIsNotInvalidated)
+{
+  readVerilogAndSetup("TestEstimateParasitics.v");
+
+  odb::dbNet* vdd = odb::dbNet::create(block_, "VDD");
+  vdd->setSpecial();
+  vdd->setSigType(odb::dbSigType::POWER);
+  int power_pins = 0;
+  for (odb::dbInst* inst : block_->getInsts()) {
+    for (odb::dbITerm* iterm : inst->getITerms()) {
+      if (iterm->getSigType() == odb::dbSigType::POWER) {
+        iterm->connect(vdd);
+        power_pins++;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  ASSERT_GT(power_pins, 0);
+  sta::Net* vdd_net = db_network_->dbToSta(vdd);
+  ASSERT_NE(vdd_net, nullptr);
+
+  ep_.setParasiticsSrc(ParasiticsSrc::kPlacement);
+  ep_.setIncrementalParasiticsEnabled(true);
+  ep_.parasiticsInvalid(vdd_net);
+  EXPECT_FALSE(ep_.hasParasiticsInvalid());
+
+  // A signal net is still pending.
+  sta::Net* d_net = flatNet(findTopPin("d"));
+  ASSERT_NE(d_net, nullptr);
+  ep_.parasiticsInvalid(d_net);
+  EXPECT_TRUE(ep_.hasParasiticsInvalid());
+  ep_.setIncrementalParasiticsEnabled(false);
+}
+
